From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: one daemon connection per output, a second output from ANLAND_SOCKET_2

Each AnlandOutput is one Android surface: its display_ctx, consumer-ready and fallback state, reconnect timer and
data/buffer-ready notifiers move from the backend into the output (AnlandOutput::Link), and its EGL layer renders
into that output's buffers. Input maps into the output's place in the layout and touch ids are offset per output,
so two Android tasks never share a touch point. Audio, camera, clipboard, keyboard visibility and the DPMS wake
stay with output 1 (the desktop).

With ANLAND_SOCKET_2 set, a second connection says hello at startup and waits on the event loop for the daemon's
screen info (connect_to_deamon in two steps: a daemon answers only once its consumer is there, maybe never). Output
"anland-2" then comes up - a PowOS window shown in its own Android task (PowosWindowActivity); KWin's output
configuration store places it (right of the desktop) and keeps its settings.
